Instrument: EO:12078\nSource: https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1978-09-07/pdf/FR-1978-09-07.pdf\nSHA-256 of the downloaded file: 7d4b86f1538e80c91f6102e020a19d5e731888c7a3db542c3dca3b1b67e53592\nLocation: 43 FR 39741, PDF pages 13-14 (confidence high)\nMachine-extracted text layer of the official PDF (OCR for 1936-1994 scans). May contain recognition errors and parts of neighbouring documents on the same pages. Not an authenticated transcription: check the PDF pages.\n\n=== PDF page 13 of 224 ===\npresidential docum ents\n[3195-01]\nExecutive Order 12078 •  September 5,1978\nPresidential Com m ission on World Hunger\n-V\nBy the authority vested in me as President by the Constitution of the  \nUnited States of America, and in order to create in accordance with the  \nFederal Advisory Committee Act (5 U.S.C. App. I) an advisory commission on  \nthe problems of hunger and malnutrition, it is hereby ordered as follows:\n1-1. Establishment o f Commission.\n1-101. There is established the Presidential Commission on World  \nHunger/\n1-102. The membership of the Commission shall be composed of not  \nmore than 20 persons from among citizens in public and private life as  \nfollows:\n(a) Sixteen members shall be appointed by the President, who shall desig­\nnate a Chairman and two Vice Chairmen.\n(b) The President of the Senate and the Speaker of the House of Repre­\nsentatives are each invited to designate two Members of their respective  \nHouses to serve on the Commission.\n1-2. Functions o f the Comm","path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/texts/EO_12078.txt","sha256":"99a6f017f11d342887ddd34de30ea8b299645eb618d15b768bfcb0154bbac212","source":{"line":1596,"path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"e1d35670aca93a3da57782a73a768e399f13691f72c2aa8e63f9b7742b3167a2"}}]}
